},{"base":"H3220","lemma":"יָם","tr":"yam","gloss":"sea","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":396},{"base":"H1992","lemma":"הֵ֫מָּה","tr":"hem·mah","gloss":"they(masc.)","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":552},{"base":"H2346","lemma":"חוֹמָה","tr":"cho·mah","gloss":"wall","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":133}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"EZK","chapter":30,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Cush, Put, and Lud, and all the various peoples, as well as Libya and the men of the covenant land, will fall with Egypt by the sword.","from":10},{"book":"EZK","chapter":38,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"Persia, Cush, and Put will accompany them, all with shields and helmets,","from":10},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"And the sons of Javan: Elishah, Tarshish, the Kittites, and the Rodanites.","from":6},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"the Arvadites, the Zemarites, and the Hamathites. Later the Canaanite clans were scattered,","from":8},{"book":"DEU","chapter":3,"verse":9,"verseEnd":9,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"which the Sidonians call Sirion but the Amorites call Senir—","from":5},{"book":"1KI","chapter":5,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"So Solomonʼs and Hiramʼs builders, along with the Gebalites, quarried the stone and prepared the timber and stone for the construction of the temple.","from":9},{"book":"ISA","chapter":2,"verse":13,"verseEnd":13,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"against all the cedars of Lebanon, lofty and lifted up, against all the oaks of Bashan,","from":6},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"And the sons of Javan: Elishah, Tarshish, the Kittites, and the Rodanites.","from":7}],"notes":[],"groups":[]},"12-25":{"people":[{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":1,"firstVerse":17},{"id":"ju