den","kind":"place","brief":"In Assyria","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"haran-h2771a","name":"Haran","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":23}],"words":[{"base":"H7402","lemma":"רָכַל","tr":"ra·khal","gloss":"to trade","lang":"h","inPassage":9,"uses":17},{"base":"H5801","lemma":"עִזָּבוֹן","tr":"iz·za·von","gloss":"ware","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":7},{"base":"H5503","lemma":"סָחַר","tr":"sa·char","gloss":"to trade","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":21},{"base":"H4627","lemma":"מַעֲרָב","tr":"ma·a·rav","gloss":"merchandise","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":9},{"base":"H7230","lemma":"רֹב","tr":"rov","gloss":"abundance","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":149},{"base":"H1992","lemma":"הֵ֫מָּה","tr":"hem·mah","gloss":"they(masc.)","lang":"h","inPassage":5,"uses":552},{"base":"H1719","lemma":"דְּדָן","tr":"de·dan","gloss":"Dedan","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H3120","lemma":"יָוָן","tr":"ya·van","gloss":"Javan","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":11},{"base":"H7553","lemma":"רִקְמָה","tr":"riq·mah","gloss":"embroidery","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":12},{"base":"H7614","lemma":"שְׁבָא","tr":"she·va","gloss":"Sheba","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":23}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"The sons of Japheth: Gomer, Magog, Madai, Javan, Tubal, Meshech, and Tiras.","from":13},{"book":"ISA","chapter":60,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"All the flocks of Kedar will be gathered to you; the rams of Nebaioth will serve you and go up on My altar with acceptance; I will adorn My glorious house.","from":21},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":3,"verseEnd":3,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The sons of Gomer: Ashkenaz, Riphath, and Togarmah.","from":14},{"book":"GEN","chapter":10,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The sons of Cush: Seba, Havilah, Sabtah, Raamah, and Sabteca. And the sons of Raamah: Sheba and Dedan.","from":22},{"book":"JDG","chapter":11,"verse":33,"verseEnd":33,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"With a great blow he devastated twenty cities from Aroer to the vicinity of Minnith, as far as Abel-keramim. So the Ammonites were subdued before the Israelites.","from":17},{"book":"2KI","chapter":19,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Did the gods of the nations destroyed by my fathers rescue those nations—the gods of Gozan, Haran, and Rezeph, and of the people of Eden in Telassar?","from":23},{"book":"ISA","chapter":2,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"against every ship of Tarshish, and against every stately vessel.","from":25},{"book":"ISA","chapter":66,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"I will establish a sign among them, and I will send survivors from among them to the nations—to Tarshish, Put, and the archers of Lud; to Tubal, Javan, and the islands far away who have not heard of My fame or seen My glory. So they will proclaim My glory among the nations.","from":13}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]},"26-36":{"people":[],"places":[{"id":"tyre-h6865","name":"Tyre","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":32}],"words":[{"base":"H4627","lemma":"מַעֲרָב","tr":"ma·a·rav","gloss":"merchandise","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":9},{"base":"H3220","lemma":"יָם","tr":"yam","gloss":"sea","lang":"h","inPassage":6,"uses":396},{"base":"H2259","lemma":"חֹבֵל","tr":"cho·vel","gloss":"pilot","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":5},{"base":"H4751","lemma":"מַר","tr":"mar","gloss":"bitter","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":37},{"base":"H4419","lemma":"מַלָּח","tr":"mal·lach","gloss":"mariner","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":4},{"base":"H5801","lemma":"עִזָּבוֹן","tr":"iz·za·von","gloss":"ware","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":7},{"base":"H1952","lemma":"הוֹן","tr":"hon","gloss":"substance","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":26},{"base":"H8432","lemma":"תָּ֫וֶךְ","tr":"ta·vekh","gloss":"midst","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":418},{"base":"H6951","lemma":"קָהָל","tr":"qa·hal","gloss":"assembly","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":123},{"base":"H7665","lemma":"שָׁבַר","tr":"sha·var","gloss":"to break","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":147}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"ISA","chapter":22,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"On that day the Lord GOD of Hosts called for weeping and wailing, for shaven heads and the wearing of sackcloth.","from":31},{"book":"JER","chapter":6,"verse":26,"verseEnd":26,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"O daughter of my people, dress yourselves in sackcloth and roll in ashes. Mourn with bitter wailing, as you would for an only son, for suddenly the destroyer will come upon us.","from":30},{"book":"JER","chapter":18,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"They have made their land a desolation, a perpetual object of scorn; all who pass by will be appalled and shake their heads.","from":36},{"book":"EZK","chapter":7,"verse":18,"verseEnd":18,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"They will put on sackcloth, and terror will overwhelm them. Shame will cover all their faces, and all their heads will be shaved.","from":31},{"book":"EXO","chapter":15,"verse":14,"verseEnd":14,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The nations will hear and tremble; anguish will grip the dwellers of Philistia.","from":28},{"book":"LEV","chapter":21,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"Priests must not make bald spots on their heads, shave off the edges of their beards, or make cuts in their bodies.","from":31},{"book":"DEU","chapter":14,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"You are sons of the LORD your God; do not cut yourselves or shave your foreheads on behalf of the dead,","from":31},{"book":"1SA","chapter":4,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"That same day a Benjamite ran from the battle line all the way to Shiloh, with his clothes torn and dirt on his head.","from":30}],"notes":[],"groups":[]}}